<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RaccoonWildTheft.xml     AnimalTheft · RIMPROPERTY_ANIMAL_THEFT_1

  Owner, 2026-09-08 (verbatim): "...as do some wild animals." Marks Core's
  own Raccoon (Defs/Core/ThingDefs_Races/Races_Animal_SquirrelGroup.xml,
  defName Raccoon) with WildTheftExtension — read directly out of the
  vanilla def, not invented. Raccoon is the obvious fit: trainability None
  (so it can never learn RM_Steal — the two theft routes stay disjoint, per
  species), and its OWN vanilla flavor text already is this feature:
  "A small, hardy animal... happy to break into your garbage container, or
  your kitchen, to eat almost anything."

  No MayRequire: Raccoon ships in Core, which is always active. Wrapped in
  PatchOperationConditional anyway (validate_patch.py's own suggested idiom,
  same shape MandrakePatches/HeadSetForFA_Revive.xml uses) purely against a
  future RimWorld version renaming or dropping the def upstream — not a
  cross-mod presence guard, since Core cannot be absent.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Raccoon"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Raccoon"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <modExtensions>
          <li Class="RimMandrake.AnimalTheft.WildTheftExtension" />
        </modExtensions>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
